  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0301' consists of four tables: 'Seat_Template', 'User', 'Seat', and 'Seat_Template_Layout'.\nThe 'Seat_Template' table represents a template for seating arrangements. It has columns for 'description', 'template_ID', and 'template_name'. 'User' table stores user information including 'contact_number', 'email', 'name', and 'user_ID'.\nThe 'Seat' table represents a seat in the venue. It has columns for 'column', 'creation_time', 'flag', 'location_X', 'location_Y', 'price', 'reservedPurchasedUserID', 'row', 'seat_ID', 'type', and 'update_time'. The 'reservedPurchasedUserID' column does not allow null values and is a foreign key referencing the 'user_ID' in the 'User' table.\nThe 'Seat_Template_Layout' table represents the layout of the seating templates. It has columns for 'occasion', 'seat_ID', 'template_ID', and 'time_period'. Both 'seat_ID' and 'template_ID' are not null and are foreign keys referencing the 'seat_ID' in the 'Seat' table and the 'template_ID' in the 'Seat_Template' table, respectively. The combination of 'seat_ID' and 'template_ID' forms the primary key of this table.\nThe schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing foreign key constraints. If a record in the 'User' table is deleted, the corresponding records in the 'Seat' table will be deleted due to the 'CASCADE' rule. Similarly, if a record in the 'Seat' table is deleted, the corresponding records in the 'Seat_Template_Layout' table will be deleted due to the 'CASCADE' rule.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirements Description:\nThis database can be used for an online seat reservation system, such as for cinemas, theaters, or conference halls. The system can record and manage seat information for different areas, including seat locations (X-coordinate, Y-coordinate, row, column), type, price, creation time, update time, etc. The system can mark the validity of seats using a flag field, such as whether a seat has been reserved or purchased. The system supports multiple seat layout templates, including template name and description, which are suitable for different occasions or time periods. Users have a unique ID, name, contact number, and email address. Users can query available seats based on seat location, type, price, etc. Users can select seats online for reservation or purchase, and the system will update the seat status accordingly.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0301.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0301\nCREATE TABLE `Seat_Template` (\n  `template_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `template_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`template_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Seat` (\n  `seat_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `row` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `column` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location_X` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location_Y` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `flag` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reservedPurchasedUserID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`seat_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `seat_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reservedPurchasedUserID`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Seat_Template_Layout` (\n  `seat_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `template_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `occasion` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time_period` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`seat_ID`, `template_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `seat_template_layout_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`seat_ID`) REFERENCES `Seat` (`seat_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `seat_template_layout_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`template_ID`) REFERENCES `Seat_Template` (`template_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
